<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan industrial output up revised 5.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan industrial output up revised 5.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in January increased a revised 5.6 percent from the previous month, compared with a preliminary estimate of a 5.3 percent increase, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>On a year-on-year comparison, industrial production in January rose a revised 8.9 percent, against a preliminary estimate of an 8.5 percent increase.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the figures:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>			  JAN     PRELIM    MONTH AGO JANINDEX</p>
<p> Output		 +5.6    +5.3    +0.1    105.8</p>
<p> Shipments	    +6.4    +5.7    -0.2    108.8</p>
<p> Inventories	   0.0     0.0    -0.4    107.0</p>
<p>Inventories-to-</p>
<p> -Shipments ratio   -3.5    -3.8    -1.0    107.8</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>			  JAN     PRELIM    MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output		 +8.9    +8.5    +3.7</p>
<p> Shipments	   +10.8   +10.1    +4.3</p>
<p> Inventories	  -2.5    -2.5    -1.9</p>
<p>Inventories-to-</p>
<p> -Shipments ratio   -9.0    -9.2    -4.4</p>
</text>
